      "worked": "The ellipse has centre $(3,1)$, horizontal radius $2$ and vertical radius $3$.\n\nTranslate 3 units left and 1 unit down. Its centre is now the origin, with radii still $2$ and $3$.\n\nDilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$, then vertically by factor $\\frac13$. Both radii become $1$, giving the unit circle.",
